# Embedded Tor (modules/expo-tor)
# Rust build artifacts, and the compiled Arti binaries. Not committed: they are
# ~7.5 MB per ABI, they are reproducible from source with `npm run
# tor:build:android` / `tor:build:ios`, and a binary blob in the tree of an
# anonymity tool is exactly the thing nobody can audit.
modules/expo-tor/rust/target/
modules/expo-tor/android/src/main/jniLibs/
modules/expo-tor/android/.gradle/
modules/expo-tor/android/build/
modules/expo-tor/ios/lib/
modules/expo-tor/ios/Pods/

# Hardhat
packages/contracts/cache/
packages/contracts/artifacts/
packages/contracts/typechain-types/
packages/contracts/deployments/localhost/

# Build outputs
dist/
build/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
# ...but share the debug targets. They encode project facts a newcomer would
# otherwise have to discover — chiefly that the static build serves on 8085,
# not the 8080 in VS Code's default template.
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/

# Logs
*.log
.vercel

# zk proving fixtures — multi-megabyte downloads, regenerate with the script
packages/contracts/inputs.json
packages/contracts/reference.json

# zk prover native output — rebuild with `npm run zk:build:android`
modules/expo-zkprove/rust/target/
modules/expo-zkprove/android/src/main/jniLibs/
modules/expo-zkprove/ios/lib/

# TypeScript project-reference build state
*.tsbuildinfo
